.TH JSON_PARSE_TEXT 3
.SH NAME
json_parse_text \- parse a JSON text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <json.h>
.P
.BI "jsonval* json_parse_text(const char* " x ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR json_parse_text ()
reads the value in the n bytes at x if json_valid(3) accepts them. Strings are stored as the text they stand for: escapes are decoded, \\uXXXX escapes (surrogate pairs too) and UTF-8 give UTF-8, and json_print writes them back.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The tree, to be released with json_free(3), or 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
json_valid(3), json_property_path(3)
